<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Hohenheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1818</span> · Also known as Hohenheim academy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of Hohenheim is a university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, housed in and around the 18th-century Hohenheim Palace. It was founded in 1818 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-wurttemberg">William I of Württemberg</a> as an agricultural school after the famine of 1816–1817, and it became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s leading agricultural colleges. It gained university status in 1967 and teaches agricultural, natural and economic sciences.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-hohenheim.jpg" alt="University of Hohenheim" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uni_Hohenheim-Logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
